# ===================================================================
# CONFIDENTIAL - NEVER PUBLISH
# ===================================================================
# private/ holds real personnel data from the 2017 migration study:
# names, document numbers and salary amounts. Ignoring the directory
# itself (not individual dataset names) means anything dropped in
# later is covered too.
#
# tests/mainframe_check.sh skips cleanly when private/ is absent, so
# a public clone still builds and passes every other suite.
private/

# ===================================================================
# BUILD OUTPUT
# ===================================================================
bin/
*.exe
*.o
*.so
*.dll
*.int
*.gnt

# ===================================================================
# TEST + SIMULATION OUTPUT
# ===================================================================
# tests/run_sim.sh regenerates these on every run.
datasets/
logs/
# Per-suite scratch areas. tests/expected/ is the committed golden
# baseline set and is deliberately NOT ignored.
tests/work/
tests/work-manual/
tests/work-mf/

# Stray DDNAME files, if a harness ever forgets to redirect one.
# Anchored to the repo root so a real file of the same name deeper
# in the tree would still be tracked.
/SYSIN
/SYSLIST
/SYSPRINT
/SYSUT1
/SYSUT2
/SYSUT3
/SYSUT4
/SYSUT5
/SYSUT6

# ===================================================================
# EDITOR / OS NOISE
# ===================================================================
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
